# Specify files that shouldn't be modified by Fern
#
# v4 starts from Fern's generated SDK rather than v3's hand-written layer. Only
# what must not be regenerated stays here:
#   .github            — the SDK Release audit fails closed unless CI is protected
#   LICENSE            — legal text, not a generated artifact
#   go.mod, go.sum     — the audit requires them, and the /v4 module path is
#                        ours to set: Go encodes the major in the module path
#   ontology.go        — hand-written: declares an ontology with structs, which
#                        the generated types cannot express
#   ontology_test.go   — its tests, which CI runs on the generated branch, so a
#                        regeneration that breaks the DSL fails its own PR
#
# Anything ported forward from v3 is re-added deliberately, file by file.
.github
LICENSE
go.mod
go.sum
.gitattributes
ontology.go
ontology_test.go
.fern/replay.lock
.fern/replay.yml
